Z||000000||Patrick86GT||05-31-2001||09:31 AM||||y 88GT has an annoying noise (rattle)at the passenger side of the rack and pinion.  I can replace it with a rebuilt unit for $130 but here's the catch. The rebuilt unit lists as fitting 86 & 87 GT's...and the parts store can't tell me if it is the same as 88. Does anyone know for sure? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||05-31-2001||10:51 AM||||Based on the examples I saw at the Swap Meet in Alabama, '88 racks are different from previous years.  Your problem may be caused by a worn rack bushing.  Rodney Dickman sells a replacement.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-31-2001||10:53 AM||||Nope. Not the same. Fiero Store <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  sells one for an 88, for $200-and-something. Rodney Dickman <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  sells the right-side bushings, if you want to rebuild it yourself..<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick86GT||05-31-2001||01:01 PM||||Thank you much!  I'll go for the rebuild it myself option!<P>Like many Fiero lovers, I could not stop at owning just one. I still have my "near-perfect" red 86GT, 4-speed and have acquired an 88GT, t-top, 5-speed for me, another 88GT auto for the little woman and another 86GT for a restoration project....Hence, I really appreciate the tech help I get from you fellows!||||reg||1
